## Conventions

- One authoritative asset per role and scope.
- Mirrors and derivatives name their upstream authority and synchronization direction.
- Retired assets remain traceable but are not presented as current.
- Group retained historical bundles by artifact family/revision or phase when useful; keep one archive route in the current index. Record the successor and old/new path map for relocated assets, without expanding default startup memory into a historical file list.
- Moves update every inbound route and trigger a stale-path search.
- Sensitive assets are represented by safe metadata and access rules, not embedded content.
- Version and revision identify the artifact family; a Git coordinate identifies provenance and does not replace either field.
